codex
Stage 1 has no two-phase lemma proof: `prove.sh` compiles `verification.k` with all 31 rules already present and then proves behavioral claims. Therefore no inventory rule qualifies as `PROVED_DERIVED_LEMMA`. I’m treating the symbolic split interception as the sole `OPERATIONAL_RULE`; it is a `<k>` execution/allocation transition, while the other 30 rules are macro, encoding, recurrence, or named-result definitions.
